{"notes":"SETTLED: 1. Score = points / taller tower height. 8 words give at most 4 colour-shape pairs, so a tall target is capped near 4/height. Confirmed: 5 blocks 0.80, 7 blocks 0.57 (several times), 9 blocks 0.44 (twice, latest round included, with 4 exact pairs). 2. Colours: dobo=green, tumu=red, zeki=yellow, nove=blue, muva=orange, tido=purple. 3. Shapes: loku=ball, vepu=ring, kuru=cube, fidi=cone, fuza=star. 4. Pair format (colour word then shape word) works. Repeated pairs and mixed sequences work. 6 words for 3 blocks gave 1.00. 5. Builder reads strictly left to right as pairs, one pair per block, stops after the pairs given. No repeat or skip markers known. 6. Builder defaults for unknown words are red cube, blue ball, or orange/purple. These are defaults, not meanings. 7. vonu, kano, mape, neto never worked as markers or as purple. Treat as unknown. Never put filler in pair slots. 8. With a tall target, use all 4 pairs on the first 4 blocks in order. This is the best achievable. 9. Both roles share the same vocabulary and pair reading, so there is no ambiguity with known words. 10. As builder, the received message this round (zeki fuza zeki fuza tido kuru nove vepu) was read as 4 pairs and built exactly, matching the target's first 4 blocks.

OPEN OR NOT WORKING: 1. Blocks beyond the 4th are unreachable with pairs. A one-word-per-block scheme is untested and the builder would not know it. 2. melu, mape, neto, kano, vonu are unassigned. They may be a sixth colour or shape, or a count marker. Nothing shown yet. 3. Later blocks of a tall target cost score and nothing seen so far fixes that.

TRY NEXT: 1. Sender with 4 or fewer blocks: known pairs, only the words needed, for 1.00. 2. Sender with a taller target: 4 known pairs on the first 4 blocks in order; expect at most 4/height. 3. Builder: read messages as colour-shape pairs. For unknown words, build a guess and log it. 4. If the target is short with spare words, test melu or neto alone in a controlled spot and log the result. 5. Log message, build, target and score each round."}

{"notes":"SETTLED: 1. Score = points / taller tower height. 8 words give at most 4 colour-shape pairs, so a target of height h is capped near 4/h. Confirmed: 4 blocks 1.00, 5 blocks 0.80, 6 blocks 0.67, 7 blocks 0.57, 8 blocks 0.50, 9 blocks 0.44, 10 blocks 0.40. 2. Colours: dobo=green, tumu=red, zeki=yellow, nove=blue, muva=orange, tido=purple. 3. Shapes: loku=ball, vepu=ring, kuru=cube, fidi=cone, fuza=star. 4. Pair format (colour word then shape word), one pair per block, read strictly left to right. Repeated pairs and mixed sequences work. The builder builds exactly the pairs given and stops. 5. Both roles share the same vocabulary, so known words are unambiguous. 6. A short message works: this round 'zeki kuru zeki kuru dobo loku' (6 words, 3 pairs) gave a perfect 1.00 on a 3-block target, so use only the words needed. 7. vonu, kano, mape, neto, melu never worked as colours or markers. Builder defaults for unknown words are red cube, blue ball, or orange/purple, and are not meanings. Never put filler in pair slots. 8. Sender can only convey the first 4 blocks. With a tall target, use all 4 pairs on the first 4 blocks in order.

OPEN OR NOT WORKING: 1. Blocks beyond the 4th are unreachable with pairs. No repeat, count, or skip marker is known, even when later blocks repeat the 4th. 2. melu, mape, neto, kano, vonu are unassigned. They may be a sixth colour or shape, or a count marker, but nothing has been shown. 3. A one-word-per-block scheme is untested and the builder would not know it.

TRY NEXT: 1. Sender with 4 or fewer blocks: known pairs, only the words needed, for 1.00. 2. Sender with a taller target: 4 known pairs on the first 4 blocks in order, expecting at most 4/height. 3. Builder: read messages as colour-shape pairs. For unknown words, build a guess and log it. 4. If the target is short with spare words, test melu or neto alone in a controlled spot (e.g. appended after complete pairs) and log the result. 5. Log message, build, target and score each round."}
